Diagnosed CSRF token mismatch in Laravel file upload request
Diagnosed CSRF token mismatch in Laravel file upload request

That 419 is the giveaway — that's Laravel's CSRF-specific status code (not raw PHP). So this is a Blade layout (@extends / @yield) with an AJAX/Promise-based file upload failing CSRF verification. 422 is separate (validation rules failing), so let's split these.

For the 419 (CSRF token mismatch) on file upload specifically:

Missing/stale meta tag in layout. Your @yield-based layout needs the token in the <head> that's actually rendered on every page that includes the upload form:
blade
<meta name="csrf-token" content="{{ csrf_token() }}">

If this meta tag lives in a partial that gets cached, or if it's in a layout section that a child view doesn't @include, the JS reads a stale/empty token.

FormData + fetch: token often silently missing. The #1 cause of 419 on file uploads specifically is that people manually append headers for JSON requests but forget it for FormData uploads, or set Content-Type manually and break the multipart boundary:
js
const formData = new FormData();
formData.append('file', fileInput.files[0]);
formData.append('_token', document.querySelector('meta[name="csrf-token"]').content);

fetch('/upload', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: formData,
    headers: {
        'X-CSRF-TOKEN': document.querySelector('meta[name="csrf-token"]').content
        // ❌ do NOT set 'Content-Type': 'multipart/form-data' manually — 
        // the browser needs to set it with the correct boundary itself
    }
})
.then(res => {
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(res.status);
    return res.json();
})
.then(data => console.log(data))
.catch(err => console.error(err));
Axios global default not set, or set too late. If you're using axios (common with SB Admin 2 dashboards), make sure this runs before any upload call, and that the meta tag actually exists in the DOM at that point:
js
axios.defaults.headers.common['X-CSRF-TOKEN'] = document.querySelector('meta[name="csrf-token"]').content;

If this JS is in a <script> at the bottom of footer.php/layout.blade.php but the upload button's page loads its own separate script that runs first (via a child @section('scripts') that gets pushed before the parent boot), the token setup hasn't run yet → undefined token → 419.

