For the 422 (validation failure):
That's just your FormRequest or $request->validate() rejecting the file — usually mimes:, max:, or a required field missing because it wasn't appended to FormData. Check your Laravel logs (storage/logs/laravel.log) — Laravel returns the exact validation errors as JSON in the response body:

js
.catch(async err => {
    const res = err.response;
    if (res && res.status === 422) {
        console.log(await res.json()); // shows exactly which field failed and why
    }
});

Fastest way to diagnose which of the above it is: open DevTools → Network tab → click the failed request → check the Request Headers for X-CSRF-TOKEN (is it present? is it undefined?) and the Payload/Form Data tab (is _token actually in there?).

